  "acceptedBoundaries": [
    "Dedicated shared Retry drains current ingestion and validates unchanged Task/Food/profile/installation identities plus protected settings and task guard; sequential Task/Food/Task reads precede clearing the stop.",
    "Retry does not append canonical bytes, retry prepared operations, reload settings, discard receipts, replace existing module handles or close editors. Hard authority/poison failures retain the stop; isolated Food history may remain module-only warning.",
    "Every Food typed-history failure is followed by shared manifest/owner revalidation before module-only propagation; missing canonical path diagnostic identifies filename without changing wire semantics.",
    "Existing private editor controllers and FocusScope subtree stay mounted under the blocking scrollable recovery overlay; Retry remains a separate fixed action.",
    "Only the first-name form keeps local typing/focus while stopped, with a bounded120px scrollable diagnostic and fixed Retry. Existing-user picker and editor command callbacks remain blocked.",
    "Explicit setup Continue captures Task/profile/name/pending identity, requires user-null and unchanged intent after shared admission, then performs captured-origin command-safety checks before/after Task refresh. Pending user IDs/names persist on failure.",
    "Module selector yields space for single/bulk Task editor IME; old header fixture prohibition is scoped to TaskToolbar while explicitly requiring the new module controls. Existing geometry/draft/canonical assertions remain."
  ],
